WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.880
So we know that the official number of Corona
virus cases is not the true number because

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.149
not everybody is being tested.

00:00:08.149 --> 00:00:13.530
And so globaly we have about 2 million cases
in the United States, it's roughly 600000

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:14.549
cases.

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:19.090
But these are the official numbers and the
official numbers are only a fraction of the

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:21.260
real number of cases.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:26.640
And as we do more testing the official number,
we'll get closer and closer to what we would

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.210
call the true number.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.800
But it still is way off.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.120
And depending on which study you look at,
it is significantly off.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:38.899
So what might the true number of Corona virus
cases be?

00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:44.120
And this is important because if way more
people have actually had it.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.039
It means it's far less deadly.

00:00:46.039 --> 00:00:50.420
It's a far lower death rate if way more people
have had corona virus.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:54.889
But it also means that it spreads much more
easily and it can impact what the plan would

00:00:54.889 --> 00:00:58.420
be or should be for starting to reopen parts
of society

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:01.260
and the economy, which Donald Trump seems
determined to do.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:06.710
And even said at yesterday's press briefing
that this week he would likely have some guidelines

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.410
or ideas about how that's all going to happen.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:11.330
So let's look at a few different data points.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:17.010
There is a town in Germany, gang guilt, and
they did a randomized sample of a thousand

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.010
residents.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:23.300
They just randomly tested a thousand people
and they found that 14 percent of the people

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.530
in Gangel had Corona virus antibodies.

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:30.860
Now, this is a comically cartoonishly high
number.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.150
And there are a few caveats.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:40.530
One is that antibody testing specifically
for this Corona virus, meaning SA's COVA too.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:46.160
It's still early and it's possible that some
of the people that tested positive for antibodies

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:51.140
have antibodies for a different corona virus
and that the test is not precisely showing

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.190
antibodies for this Corona virus combined
with

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:58.050
Gangel being a center of infection.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:02.810
So it's unlikely 14 percent of the world has
been infected.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:08.340
Of course, if the real infection rate were
14 percent in Germany, that would imply as

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.390
many as 11 million people in Germany had the
virus.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:17.030
The official number is only 128 thousand if
it's anywhere close to accurate.

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:22.590
We're talking about drastically different
infection rates than the official numbers.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:28.630
But there are multiple reasons to significantly
question whether 14 percent is really the

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:29.710
right number.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:31.830
We have another data point from Austria.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.630
Austria tested 15 100 people.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.760
It was a representative sample of the population.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:43.510
And they found that looking at a confidence
interval somewhere between point 12 and point

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:48.270
seventy six percent of the population had
the virus.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:53.700
Now, that's a pretty wide confidence interval
because the official case number in Austria

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:59.680
is fourteen thousand point 12 percent of the
population would be fewer people.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:00.680
It's only

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.540
10000 Austrians.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:06.680
If you go to point 76, that's like sixty seven
thousand Austrians.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.980
So, again, we don't know.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:15.980
It seems that according to this test, the
true rate in Austria is somewhere between

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:20.170
the official rate and five times the official
rate.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:26.480
Very different numbers than that sample from
Germany, where 14 percent supposedly had the

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:27.480
antibodies.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:31.520
Then here in Massachusetts, we have a totally
different type of test that was done, a sewage

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.810
analysis.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:34.360
This is not an exact science.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:36.210
Nobody is pretending that it is.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:43.880
The sewage analysis suggests that a region
here in New England with 500 official cases

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:50.239
estimates that the real number of cases could
be anywhere from 20, 300 to 150000.

00:03:50.239 --> 00:03:54.819
And again, these are wacky, large confidence
intervals.

00:03:54.819 --> 00:04:03.209
This would imply that the real rate is anywhere
from five times to 250 times the official

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.209
number.

00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:06.500
It's almost impossible to believe that

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:11.000
the real number might be 250 times the official
case number.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:17.370
That would imply 143 million cases in the
United States seems inconceivable, but certainly

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:24.370
5x the official number 10x the official number
may be 20 x the official number, if there

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:28.400
are really a ton of asymptomatic cases, could
be possible.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.310
That's data point number three.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:35.500
And then lastly, we have a study which suggests
the detection rate is 6 percent.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:43.389
So if we're detecting 6 percent of the cases,
that would imply the real rate is about 16

00:04:43.389 --> 00:04:45.710
times higher than the official rate.

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:51.140
Once again, that would suggest we've had 10
million infections in the United States instead

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:52.800
of 600000.

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:58.420
So the real answer right now is we don't know
the amount that we don't know about the spread

00:04:58.420 --> 00:04:59.420
ability and.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:06.360
Other factors about this particular coronavirus
is huge, and every day I'm reading pre-print

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:07.360
of soon

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:10.970
to be published, peer reviewed studies, many
conflict with each other.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:18.280
As an example, there's a new one that suggests
that the way that Corona virus is initially

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:25.949
hurting people is actually by reducing blood
oxygen supply rather than being a primary

00:05:25.949 --> 00:05:33.040
in respiratory illness, and that what is initially
a low oxygen level in blood is leading to

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:34.430
respiratory symptoms.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:40.290
Again, this stuff in retrospect, we're going
to figure it out as we get closer to a vaccine,

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:45.760
as we continue to learn about which therapeutic
treatments will work better.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:49.280
But there is so much that we just don't don't
know right now.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:53.720
And that is part of what makes this so difficult,
which is when we say look at the curve, look

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:56.910
at how it's starting to plateau and go down.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:06:01.370
We don't know the effect of whether there
are conflicting studies about temperature

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:02.540
and humidity.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:04.790
There's just so much that we don't know.

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:09.350
And we will learn it in retrospect and hopefully
in time for Wave 2 and possibly what we'll

00:06:09.350 --> 00:07:22.070
be wave 3.

